# The ledger is the one file in this repository that must never be resolved by
# picking a side. Rows are experiments, N is the denominator of every
# multiple-testing correction, and taking one machine's file silently discards
# the other machine's questions with nothing downstream to say so. The driver
# unions them on the table's own UNIQUE key.
#
# Run #19 is why this exists: the worker computed 112 trials over 39 minutes,
# hit a conflict on a report file during `git pull --rebase`, and lost them.
ledger/trials.sqlite merge=orcledger -text

# Reports are DERIVED. Every cycle regenerates them from the ledger, so a
# conflict here has no information in it -- keeping either side is correct and
# the next cycle overwrites both. `ours` keeps what is already on the branch
# being rebased onto, which is the version already published.
reports/*.json merge=ours
reports/*.md   merge=ours

# Text files this project writes on Windows and the runner reads on Linux.
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
